    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "apU-N7Hq22RF"
      },
      "source": [
        "We found `class_weight=\"balanced\"` barely changed PR-AUC (0.3510 to\n",
        "0.3556) because PR-AUC is threshold-independent: it measures ranking\n",
        "quality, and the model's underlying ability to order transactions by fraud\n",
        "likelihood didn't meaningfully improve. What changed is the fitted decision\n",
        "boundary: reweighting the loss to counter the 0.386% imbalance pushed far\n",
        "more predicted probabilities above the fixed 0.5 threshold, trading\n",
        "precision for recall at a poor exchange rate. Recall more than quadrupled\n",
        "(0.182 to 0.780), but precision fell by a factor of roughly 39 (0.686 to\n",
        "0.018) — 570 predicted positives became 95,303. F2 weights recall more\n",
        "heavily than precision but still requires some minimum precision to\n",
        "combine meaningfully with recall; at 0.018 precision, F2 collapses to\n",
        "0.0805 despite the recall gain. MCC falls even further, to 0.1005, since it\n",
        "penalizes false positives and false negatives symmetrically, and 93,630\n",
        "false positives is enough to swamp the improvement from 1,282 additional\n",
        "true positives caught (391 to 1,673). Operationally, we'd need a review\n",
        "team to manually check 95,303 flagged transactions to find 1,673 real\n",
        "frauds — not a usable trade at this fraud rate, even though it \"catches\n",
        "more fraud\" on paper."
      ],
      "id": "apU-N7Hq22RF"
    },
