      "source": [
        "# alpha=0.25 (the RetinaNet default) applies LESS weight to the rare fraud\n",
        "# class here, which fights against the whole point of using focal loss on an\n",
        "# imbalanced problem. Testing a range of alpha values instead of assuming\n",
        "# one, same as every other design decision we made in this project.\n",
        "\n",
        "def train_focal(alpha, gamma=2.0, epochs=200, lr=0.01, seed=42):\n",
        "    torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "    model = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(X_train_t.shape[1], 1), nn.Sigmoid())\n",
        "    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=lr)\n",
        "    for epoch in range(epochs):\n",
        "        optimizer.zero_grad()\n",
        "        y_pred = model(X_train_t)\n",
        "        loss = focal_loss(y_pred, y_train_t, alpha=alpha, gamma=gamma)\n",
        "        loss.backward()\n",
        "        optimizer.step()\n",
        "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
        "        proba = model(X_test_t).numpy().ravel()\n",
        "    pred = (proba >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"alpha\": alpha,\n",
        "        \"predicted_positives\": int(pred.sum()),\n",
        "        \"PR-AUC\": average_precision_score(y_test, proba),\n",
        "        \"F2\": fbeta_score(y_test, pred, beta=2),\n",
        "        \"MCC\": matthews_corrcoef(y_test, pred),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "results = [train_focal(a) for a in [0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95]]\n",
        "pd.DataFrame(results)\n"
      ],
      "id": "MfO2DC_w22RH"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RVm4gKNt22RH"
      },
      "source": [
        "PR-AUC rises steadily as we increase alpha (0.3482, 0.3503, 0.3538,\n",
        "0.3577, 0.3583), confirming our theory: giving more weight to the fraud\n",
        "class through `alpha_t` steadily improves the model's underlying ranking\n",
        "ability. F2 and MCC stay at essentially zero through alpha=0.75 — one lone\n",
        "predicted positive appears at that point, and it happens to be wrong, which\n",
        "is enough to nudge MCC very slightly negative (-0.0001) rather than exactly\n",
        "zero. The real transition happens between alpha=0.75 and alpha=0.9, where\n",
        "predicted positives jump from 1 to 1,429 and F2/MCC move immediately off\n",
        "zero rather than climbing gradually.\n",
        "\n",
        "At `alpha=0.9` (PR-AUC 0.3577, F2 0.3837, MCC 0.4369), Focal Loss beats our\n",
        "Control on all three metrics simultaneously — the only strategy we tested\n",
        "here that does that. Class Weights and SMOTE both traded a lot of MCC for a\n",
        "modest PR-AUC gain; Focal Loss at this alpha instead improves PR-AUC\n",
        "modestly while lifting both F2 and MCC well above Control. At `alpha=0.95`\n",
