    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "k5JVUjiu22RK"
      },
      "source": [
        "We found SMOTE behaves very differently from Class Weights on Random\n",
        "Forest, breaking a pattern we established with Logistic Regression. There,\n",
        "SMOTE and Class Weights converged to nearly identical results, because both\n",
        "are mechanically similar ways of reweighting a single linear decision\n",
        "boundary. For Random Forest they diverge sharply: Class Weights left\n",
        "PR-AUC, F2, and MCC essentially unchanged from Control, while SMOTE moved\n",
        "all three, and not uniformly for the better. Recall rose substantially\n",
        "(0.7170 to 0.8396: 263 more true frauds caught, TP 1,538 to 1,801) at a\n",
        "real cost to precision (0.8418 to 0.5542: 1,160 more false positives, FP\n",
        "289 to 1,449) — predicted positives nearly doubled (1,827 to 3,250). Under\n",
        "F2, which weights recall more heavily, this trade nets positive (0.7389 to\n",
        "0.7612). Under MCC, which penalizes false positives and false negatives\n",
        "symmetrically, it nets negative (0.7761 to 0.6807) — the additional false\n",
        "positives outweigh the value of the additional true positives from a\n",
        "balanced-error perspective.\n",
        "\n",
        "We think the PR-AUC drop (0.8146 to 0.7458) is the more telling signal,\n",
        "since PR-AUC is threshold-independent: it is not measuring where the fixed\n",
        "0.5 cutoff happens to land, but the model's ranking quality across every\n",
        "possible threshold. A drop of this size means SMOTE produced a genuinely\n",
        "worse-ranking model overall, not merely a different operating point on the\n",
        "same underlying curve. Our best explanation is that SMOTE interpolates\n",
        "linearly between minority-class neighbors across every feature, including\n",
        "ones that are naturally binary or near-discrete (`is_night`, `gender_flag`,\n",
        "and `category_risk`'s finite set of category-level values), producing\n",
        "synthetic points with fractional values that correspond to no real\n",
        "transaction. We think a high-capacity, non-linear model like Random Forest\n",
        "can fit spurious local structure around this synthetic noise in a way a\n",
        "single global linear boundary largely cannot, which would explain why\n",
        "SMOTE degraded Random Forest's ranking ability here but left Logistic\n",
        "Regression's comparatively unaffected."
      ],
      "id": "k5JVUjiu22RK"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
