      "source": [
        "We deliberately left Focal Loss out of this comparison. It is a\n",
        "loss-reweighting technique — `alpha_t * (1-p_t)^gamma * log(p_t)` —\n",
        "defined for models trained by gradient descent on a differentiable loss\n",
        "function. We can't train Random Forest that way: each tree is grown by\n",
        "greedily choosing splits that maximize impurity reduction (Gini or entropy)\n",
        "at each node, with no loss function being minimized across the ensemble at\n",
        "all. We don't see a meaningful way to substitute focal loss into that\n",
        "process without changing what \"Random Forest\" means, so rather than force\n",
        "an approximate substitute into this slot, we leave it out and disclose it\n",
        "as a genuine boundary of this comparison: Focal Loss's benefit is specific\n",
        "to gradient-optimized models, and this section can only test whether\n",
        "Control, Class Weights, and SMOTE generalize across model types."
      ],
      "id": "vrfJKAXy22RL"
